@startuml 21_state_document_version
!include _style.iuml
title State Machine Diagram (4/5) — DocumentVersion and its ObjectRecord (knowledge ingestion)

state "DocumentVersion" as DV {
  [*] --> STAGED : stage_version\n[type, signature, size ok]\n/ object QUARANTINED
  STAGED --> READY : process_version\n[hash ok ∧ parsed ∧ embeddings complete]\n/ object CLEAN
  STAGED --> FAILED : parse / integrity / embedding error
  READY --> Published : publish [CAS on document.version]\n/ published_version_id = this
  state Published : current version for retrieval
  Published --> READY : another version published
  Published --> REVOKED : revoke document\n/ pointer cleared, readers lose access
  READY --> REVOKED : revoke
  FAILED --> [*]
  REVOKED --> [*]
}

note right of DV
  A failed V2 never replaces an active V1.
  Retrieval only reads published READY versions
  whose object is CLEAN (ACL filter before ranking).
end note
@enduml
